%N A398863 Numbers with ordered prime signature (1,1,2).
%C A398863 Sphenic numbers multiplied by their greatest prime factor.
%C A398863 Proper subset of A085987.
%C A398863 A008479(a(n)) >= 4.
%H A398863 Michael De Vlieger, <a href="/A398863/b398863.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398863 <a href="/index/Pri#prime_signature">Index to sequences related to prime signature</a>
%e A398863 Table of n, a(n) for select n:
%e A398863     n     a(n)
%e A398863   ----------------------------
%e A398863     1     150 = 2 * 3 * 5^2
%e A398863     2     294 = 2 * 3 * 7^2
%e A398863     3     490 = 2 * 5 * 7^2
%e A398863     4     726 = 2 * 3 * 11^2
%e A398863     5     735 = 3 * 5 * 7^2
%e A398863     6    1014 = 2 * 3 * 13^2
%e A398863     7    1210 = 2 * 5 * 11^2
%e A398863     8    1690 = 2 * 5 * 13^2
%e A398863    11    1815 = 3 * 5 * 11^2
%e A398863    22    4235 = 5 * 7 * 11^2
%e A398863    55   13013 = 7 * 11 * 13^2
%e A398863   128   41327 = 11 * 13 * 17^2
%p A398863 q:= n-> is([1$2, 2]=sort(ifactors(n)[2])[.., 2]):
%p A398863 select(q, [$1..10120])[];  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Aug 16 2026
%t A398863 Select[Range[11000], FactorInteger[#][[;; , -1]] == {1, 1, 2} &]
%o A398863 (Python)
%o A398863 from math import isqrt
%o A398863 from sympy import primepi, primerange
%o A398863 from oeis_sequences.OEISsequences import bisection
%o A398863 def A398863(n):
%o A398863     def f(x): return n+x-sum(primepi(k) if (k:=x//(p**2*q))<q else j for p in primerange(isqrt(x)+1) for j, q in enumerate(primerange(min((x//p**2)+1,p))))
%o A398863     return bisection(f,n,n) # _Chai Wah Wu_, Aug 20 2026
